            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Today (Monday, **August 3, 2026**), the most notable *Azure / Azure AI–adjacent* news items are:\n\n- **ArcelorMittal expands its partnership with Microsoft, naming Azure as its primary cloud and leaning into AI-led transformation.** This is being reported across multiple outlets today and is framed around scaling data + AI capabilities on Azure across global operations. ([thenextweb.com](https://thenextweb.com/news/arcelormittal-microsoft-azure-primary-cloud-ai))\n\n- **Recent (last few days) “Foundry” ecosystem distribution news:** Moonshot AI’s **Kimi K3** is reported to be reaching enterprise users **via Fireworks on Microsoft Foundry**, which matters for Azure AI customers because it expands managed model-access pathways in the Foundry ecosystem. ([technode.com](https://technode.com/2026/07/30/moonshot-ais-kimi-k3-reaches-enterprise-users-through-fireworks-on-microsoft-foundry/))\n\nIf you mean **product/feature releases “today” inside Azure AI** (not press/customer stories), the most reliable places are Microsoft’s official feeds:\n- **Azure Updates** (filter for AI services / Azure AI / Foundry / Azure OpenAI as needed). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n- **Azure Blog (AI tag)** and **Announcements** page for official writeups. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/tag/ai/))\n\nTell me which you want and I’ll narrow it down:\n1) **Azure AI Foundry / Azure OpenAI feature releases**, or  \n2) **Customer/partner news using Azure AI**, or  \n3) **Security/governance news related to enterprise AI on Azure**.",
